%N A089929 Algebraic degree of cot(Pi/n).
%C A089929 Also the algebraic degrees of the surface area and volume of an n-prism with unit edge lengths.
%C A089929 For c = cot(Pi/n) and z = exp(2*Pi*i/n), z = (c+i)/(c-i), so Q(c,i) = Q(z,i) = Q(exp(2*Pi*i/lcm(n,4))). Since c is real, a(n) = phi(lcm(n,4))/2 = phi(n/gcd(n,2)). - _Eric W. Weisstein_, Oct 08 2026
%C A089929 For the summatory asymptotic, split the sum into odd k, where a(k) = phi(k), and even k, where a(k) = phi(k/2). The corresponding main terms are 2*n^2/Pi^2 and 3*n^2/(4*Pi^2). - _Eric W. Weisstein_, Oct 08 2026
%H A089929 Jon Maiga, <a href="/A089929/b089929.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 2..400</a>
%H A089929 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/Cotangent.html">Cotangent</a>.
%H A089929 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/Prism.html">Prism</a>.
%H A089929 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/RegularPolygon.html">Regular Polygon</a>.
%F A089929 a(n) = A000010(n/gcd(n, 2)). - _Jon Maiga_, Sep 01 2019 [Proved by _Eric W. Weisstein_, Oct 08 2026]
%F A089929 Sum_{k=2..n} a(k) ~ 11*n^2/(4*Pi^2). - _Amiram Eldar_, Sep 08 2026 [Proved by _Eric W. Weisstein_, Oct 08 2026]
%t A089929 a[n_] := Exponent[ MinimalPolynomial[ Cot[Pi/n]][x], x]; Table[ a[n], {n, 2, 52}] (* _Jean-François Alcover_, Oct 03 2012 *)
%t A089929 (* Alternative: *)
%t A089929 Table[EulerPhi[n/GCD[n, 2]], {n, 2, 21}] (* _Eric W. Weisstein_, Oct 08 2026 *)
